ry weird backstory  he's from outer space he's Friends of  Nazis and runs a monster society  sometimes it can even eat dimensions  after Savannah returns to the rock of  eternity as an adult and defeats the  wizard Shazam he  only less the seven deadly enemies of  man escape that mr. mind also breaks out  setting up the weirdest mid-credits  scene of all time  young Billy Batson is separated from his  teenage mother after she fails to win  him a stuffed tiger at a carnival  later on Shazam hands a tiger doll to a  terrified young girl to calm her there  are Tigers on Shazam's costume so what's  up with all these Tigers as always  there's a reason rooted in comics one of  Billy's best friends is a talking tiger  obviously that tiger mr. talkie Tony  first appeared in 1947 Captain Marvel  Adventures issues 79 where it was  revealed that he's just an ordinary  tiger who really really wanted to wear  clothes and eat ice cream after  consuming a brain energizing serum why  does he need his fancy brain potion to  defend himself against a murder he'd  been accused of of course it's all weird  Tony hops on a boat and shows up in the  city where everyone is terrified of free  roaming Tigers even when they politely  ask questions all this resolved however  when Captain Marvel secures Tony a job  as a museum guide Paul's well that ends  well and Tony has given a place among  the Marvel family if we already have  talking worms talking Tigers can't be  that far behind  and speaking of talking animals  somewhere on the rock of eternity  there's a giant cavern full of doors two  different worlds one door in particular  opens up to crocodiles playing poker and  they aren't just an invention for the  movie the crocodile men from the planet  punkers first showed up in the early  days of Captain Marvel adventures and  half names like Sylvester Herkimer and  jock working alongside mr. mind and his  monster Society of evil much later in  2006 a talking croc named Sobek shows up  and a few weeks later a longtime Shazam  villain Black Adam tears him apart and  makes boots out of his skin so no matter  how you look at it those cardsharp crocs  were actually kind of a big deal and  they'll probably be back for more even  though dr. sivana and mr. mind are some  of Shazam's most memorable foes there's  one that's even more notable black Adam  DC announced Black Adam solo movie in  January of 2017 and it was supposed to  show up before Shazam so what gives the  wizard Shazam mentions in the film that  he had a previous champion who'd  betrayed him and there's little doubt  that he's referring to Black Adam in the  original comic books Black Adam is given  powers of the six ancient gods but uses  some selfishly so the wizard banishes  Black Adam to outer space adam spends  5,000 years trying to make it back to  earth and when he does he jealously  terrorizes billy batson for many more  decades so even though we've set up for  a mr. mind serve on a team up in Shazam  - it's a good bet that the Wizards old  champion will be showing up for a fight  - Shazam has been described as Superman  meets big am a comparison couldn't  possibly be more appropriate especially  after seeing one specific scene in the  movie well Tom Hanks and Robert loggia  may enjoy a charming duet in the middle  of fao schwarz on a king-sized floor  piano and big Shazam gives its own spin  on the scene of drawing a shopping mall  battle between Shazam and Savannah while  they don't quite make the same beautiful  music together the colossal piano they  wind up fighting on drives the  connection home and if you're looking  for truly vintage references look no  further than the iconic cover of 1945  Superman issue 32 where Superman shrugs  off lightning bolts with a casual it  tickles similar words are spoken by  Shazam while bullets bounce off of em  really bringing home that this guy is as  powerful as a Big Blue Boy Scout check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more lo